# Copy this file to client/.env.local (that name is git-ignored) and fill in
# what you need. Restart `npx expo start` after changing it.

# Where the app should find the Express server.
#
# Leave it unset for normal development: the app works out the address by
# itself (localhost on web, your laptop's network address in Expo Go, and
# 10.0.2.2 in the Android emulator). See client/src/config/api.ts.
#
# Set it when the phone cannot reach your laptop directly, for example:
#   - on campus Wi-Fi, which blocks phone-to-laptop connections:
#       run `ngrok http 3000` and paste the https URL it prints
#   - on a phone hotspot: your laptop's address on the hotspot, e.g. http://172.20.10.2:3000
#   - when using `npx expo start --tunnel`
#   - when the server is deployed somewhere
#
# Include http:// or https://. A trailing /api/v1 is optional.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://example.ngrok-free.app
